"""Approximate a sparse parenthesized-number / boundary response.

Digits starting a parenthesis are negative near the document's beginning
and in CJK enumerations, particularly at a new line. A separately tokenized
closing parenthesis repeats the response for single-digit labels. Ordinary
numeric parentheses are weakly positive. TeX boxed answers are positive.
Document-opening syntax and token-shape classes have separate boundary
values. Backslash-prefixed tokens, @ markers and chat/tool boundaries get
small offsets. At line starts, closing responses weaken as more numbered
parentheses occur. Most token-specific variation is not modeled.
State (recent text, position and numbering count) resets each document.
